# Bounded Contexts and REST

Each service owns its Mongo DB (`identity`, `catalog`, `cart`, `inventory`, `order`, `payment`, `review`). Do not query another service's collection.

## Public surface (gateway → `/api/**`)

| Area | Paths |
|---|---|
| Auth | `/api/auth/register\|login\|google\|refresh\|logout`, `/api/me` |
| Catalog | `/api/categories`, `/api/products`, `/api/products/{slug}` |
| Cart | `/api/cart` (guestToken query for guests) |
| Checkout | `/api/checkout/sessions`, `/api/orders` |
| Reviews | `/api/reviews`, `/api/products/{id}/reviews` |
| Webhook | `/api/webhooks/stripe` (no JWT; signature / event id) |
| Admin | `/api/admin/**` — `ADMIN` role via `UserContextResolver` |

Add new public paths by updating **both** the service controller and `gateway/src/main/resources/application.yml` routes. Route order matters: more specific paths (e.g. `/api/products/*/reviews`) before catch-alls.

## Internal surface (`/internal/**`)

Service-to-service only. Protected by `InternalKeyFilter`. Gateway must not proxy these.

Typical: catalog product-by-id + rating rollup · inventory reserve/confirm/release + stock batch · cart get/clear by user · payment session · order mark-paid + verified-purchase.

## Invariants

- **identity** — JWT access (~15m) + refresh cookie (7d). Roles `CUSTOMER` / `ADMIN`.
- **catalog** — unique `slug`; no stock; rating fields updated only via internal rollup.
- **inventory** — atomic reserve; confirm decrements onHand; release restores reserved.
- **cart** — user or guest; merge on login; validate product + available qty.
- **order** — status `PENDING_PAYMENT` → `CONFIRMED` → `PACKED` → `SHIPPED` → `DELIVERED` / `CANCELLED`.
- **payment** — Stripe event id unique (`processed_events`) for idempotency.
- **review** — one review per user+product; verified purchase via order internal API.

Shop availability: catalog may batch `GET /internal/stock?productIds=`. On failure, omit the badge — do not fail the listing.
